course: dictionary
lesson: 4637
title: Hinge: a joint and a dependence
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hinge is a small metal joint that lets a door, gate, lid or window swing open and shut. You can find hinges on cupboards, boxes and laptop screens too. A door can only swing because the hinge holds its edge in one place.
explain: Hinge can also be a verb. «Everything hinges on the weather» means the whole plan depends on the weather: if the weather changes, everything changes. The words around it give the clue: everything, and the weather, show that something depends on something else.
explain: Your body has hinges too. «The elbow and knee are hinges like a door», so they bend and straighten the way a door swings. «The lower jaw... swings on a hinge just in front of each ear», so put your fingers there and open your mouth to feel it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «The lower jaw swings on a hinge», a small joint fits, so hinge means a joint. In «Everything hinges on the weather», a metal joint does not fit, but depends on does, so here hinges means depends on.
fact: A hinge is a small metal joint that lets a door, gate, lid or window swing open and shut.
fact: As a verb, «hinge on» means to depend completely: «Everything hinges on the weather».
fact: «The lower jaw swings on a hinge just in front of each ear.»
fact: The elbow and knee are hinge joints, and they move like a door.
fact: Safety: fingers can get trapped in the hinge side of a door, so keep your fingers clear when a door swings.
exercise: «The lower jaw swings on a hinge just in front of each ear.» What is a hinge here? | A sharp pain in the ear | *A small joint that lets something swing | A loud noise | A kind of cloud
exercise: Ella says «Everything hinges on the weather». What does hinges mean here? | Swings open and shut | Is made of metal | *Depends completely on | Gets wet
exercise: Which joint in your body works like a door hinge? | The neck | The hip | The shoulder | *The knee
test: In «The whole plan hinges on your help», which word is the best swap for hinges? | Opens | Squeaks | *Depends | Shines
test: Which of these is a hinge? | A cup on a table | A cloud in the sky | A dog's bark | *The small metal joint on a gate that lets it swing
exam: Jayden says the hinge in «The lower jaw swings on a hinge» is a bone. What is the best answer? | No, a hinge is only found on doors | Yes, because the jaw is a hinge | Yes, the hinge is the bone itself | *No, a hinge is the joint where the bone swings
